/**
 * Stylix Color Scheme for Rofi
 *
 * This file is auto-generated when using the NixOS/Stylix integration.
 * Do not edit manually — changes will be overwritten on system rebuild.
 *
 * To use this color scheme:
 *   1. Set "color_scheme": "stylix" in your user_config.json or defaults.json
 *   2. Enable the rofi-suite Home Manager module:
 *        programs.rofi-suite = {
 *          enable = true;
 *          useStylixColors = true;
 *        };
 *   3. The module generates this file from your Stylix base16 palette
 *
 * Base16 Color Mapping (defaults — customizable via colorMapping option):
 *   base00 → background     (default background)
 *   base01 → background-alt (lighter background, inputbar, alternate rows)
 *   base05 → foreground     (default text color)
 *   base0D → selected       (selection highlight — typically blue)
 *   base0B → active         (active state — typically green)
 *   base08 → urgent         (urgent state — typically red)
 *
 * For non-Nix users: this file is a placeholder. Choose any color scheme
 * from templates/colors/ (e.g., nord, dracula, catppuccin) or define
 * your own following the 6-variable format above.
 */
